====================================================================
Reaper build — licensing notice for the Reaper modifications
====================================================================

This file is a SECONDARY notice that applies specifically to the
"Reaper" modifications to Asuswrt-Merlin. It does NOT replace or
weaken the primary license: the base project and this derivative
work are governed by the GNU General Public License, version 2, the
full text of which is in the root file `LICENSE`. In any conflict,
the GPL v2 in `LICENSE` and the applicable upstream copyrights
control. This notice only clarifies how the Reaper-authored portions
are licensed and what is NOT covered.


1. What "the Reaper modifications" are
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The Reaper build ("Reaper") is a security-hardened, single-model
derivative of Asuswrt-Merlin (RMerl/asuswrt-merlin.ng), itself a
derivative of ASUS's Asuswrt GPL release, for the ASUS RT-BEXXU.

"The Reaper modifications" means the original work authored for
Reaper and distributed in this repository, including but not limited
to:

  - the security-hardening changes to the open-source userspace,
    distributed as the patch series in `patches/`;
  - the Hardware QoS engines (`qos_type=10` and the `qos_type=11`
    Classful engine, QoS v3/v4);
  - the Traffic Analyzer collector (`rtrafd`) and its web page;
  - the AI Advisor read-only LAN MCP server (`rmcpd`) and its
    arming/enrollment control plane;
  - the Reaper user-interface rebrand/redesign and the serve-time
    theme injection; and
  - the project documentation in this repository authored for Reaper.


